      "final_message": "When `service.checkout(\"7781\")` runs, the key written to the audit log is `AUD-ORDER-7781`.\n\n1. `service.checkout` calls `write_audit(\"order\", \"7781\")` in `audit.py`.\n2. The tool output hid the line in `write_audit` that builds the key (it showed as `[REDACTED:SECRET]`), so I couldn't read it directly. I ran the function instead, and it produced `AUD-ORDER-7781`.\n3. That result matches `_format_key`, which builds `f\"{AUDIT_PREFIX}-{kind.upper()}-{ident}\"` using `AUDIT_PREFIX = \"AUD\"` from `config.py`.\n\n`decoy_metrics.py` looks similar but builds `MET-...` keys for a metrics dict and never writes to the audit log. `decoy_cache.py` doesn't touch the audit log either.\n\nANSWER: AUD-ORDER-7781",
